WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:03.610
Ok so The Last Of Us is probably my favourite
game of all time.

00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:07.069
I think it's something that transcends the
medium and that it stands toe to toe with

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:09.230
the best movies and tv shows.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.769
It's easy to see why HBO have developed it
into one and throughout this video I'm gonna

00:00:13.769 --> 00:00:18.060
be discussing why the game's ending is something
that has stuck with me since it first released

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.450
all the way back in 2013.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:24.630
It's a game that I've completed multiple times
and everytime there's a remaster or remake

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:28.080
it's something I pick up day one just so I
can go back to it.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:32.279
Though overall the gameplay is pretty straight
forward, what really elevates the Last Of

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:34.810
Us is it's character development and story.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:38.730
Over the shoulder third person survival horror
games had become a staple of the industry

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.850
after the release of Resident Evil 4 and though
the Last Of Us doesn't really break the mould

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:47.800
when it comes to that, the characters go above
and beyond to elevate the entire experience.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.920
The ending is no different and what really
pushes it is the fact that very few words

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:56.010
are spoken between the characters but you
can see instantly what's going on beneath

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.160
the surface.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.260
Performance capture in video games is something
that's came a long way over the last couple

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:06.070
of decades and we've pretty much watched games
evolve from 2D sprites to living breathing

00:01:06.070 --> 00:01:11.180
people who can portay their deepest thoughts
in their expressions and body language.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:15.800
The Last Of Us capitalises on this massively
and Naughty Dog arguably helped to pioneer

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:19.830
the cinematic experience in video games.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:23.890
Games have always been criticised for their
storytelling but here was a studio that put

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.259
that above all else and the game excels because
of it.

00:01:27.259 --> 00:01:30.610
Whenever I've talked about the ending of the
Last Of Us I've always referred to it as being

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.920
The Godfather of gaming.

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:36.610
Now what I mean by that is that it is very
similar to the ending of another of my favourites,

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:37.670
The Godfather.

00:01:37.670 --> 00:01:42.259
In that we see Michael Corleone descend to
new depths and he has his sisters husband

00:01:42.259 --> 00:01:44.080
killed for betraying the family.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:48.869
His girlfriend Kay goes to him and after Michaels
sister barges in and reveals the truth Michael

00:01:48.869 --> 00:01:52.399
lies about it in order to not destroy the
image Kay has of him.

00:01:52.399 --> 00:01:56.500
However from the final shot you very much
get the idea that she knows the truth but

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:00.640
that she's willing to accept the lie but the
reality is too horrifying to bear.

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:05.060
We watch the door close on her and it's somethign
that still gives me goosebumps today due to

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:06.980
the symbolism carried in it.

00:02:06.980 --> 00:02:11.350
The ending of The Last Of Us is in the same
vein with Joel lying to Ellie and we see as

00:02:11.350 --> 00:02:15.910
she very much has to force herself to believe
it because the alternative is too devastating

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:16.910
to accept.

00:02:16.910 --> 00:02:20.390
We're very much left wondering if the person
we've followed throughout the entire story

00:02:20.390 --> 00:02:24.569
is actually the good guy we were led to believe
they are and it leaves us questioning the

00:02:24.569 --> 00:02:27.220
final few moments over and over.

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:31.580
We've spent hours and hours being Joel and
putting ourselves in his shoes.

00:02:31.580 --> 00:02:35.790
We've grown a bond with the guy and seeing
him lie here is completely understandable

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.091
even if we don't totally condone it.

00:02:37.091 --> 00:02:41.650
It really speaks to how complex the game is
as a whole and the entire thing operates in

00:02:41.650 --> 00:02:42.690
shades of grey.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:47.190
Now in order to get to this point and all
that it means we have to talk about the steps

00:02:47.190 --> 00:02:48.190
that got us there.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:53.080
This all happens because of the opening of
the game which completely defines Joels life.

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:57.610
In it we watch Joel and his Daugther Sarah
on the night of the Cordyseps outbreak.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:01.640
After a rather laidback introductory scene,
you're thrown in at the deepend and from the

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:05.360
perspective of Sarah you watch the world descend
into chaos.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.180
No one knows what is going on and in this
panic the car their in with Joels brother

00:03:09.180 --> 00:03:11.610
Tommy is forced off the road.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:16.129
Sarah's unable to properly walk and Joel has
to carry her through the streets as the infected

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.319
to start to swarm them.

00:03:17.319 --> 00:03:21.470
They come across a lone soldier and whilst
this would normally be a sign of safety in

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.180
any other situation like this The Last Of
Us twists the scenario.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:30.170
Ordered to kill the pair the soldier fires
on them and he hits Sarah.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:34.330
She dies in Joels arm in a moment that will
completely rip your heart out of your chest

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:37.349
and it's arguably the most impactful game
opening of all time.

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:42.050
Now from here we get a twenty year time jump
and pick up with Joel living in a Fedra outpost.

00:03:42.050 --> 00:03:46.489
Working as a smuggler with his girlfriend
Tess we very much get the idea throughout

00:03:46.489 --> 00:03:50.170
the game that Joel has had to do horrendous
things to survive.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:53.640
This drove a wedge between him and his brother
and it seems like he's a complete shell of

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:54.640
the person that he used to be.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:55.640
Due to the loss that Joel faced that night
he's cut himself off emotionally so that he

00:03:55.640 --> 00:03:56.640
doesn't have to face the emotional toil that
that took on him.

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.730
Joels entire outlook is based around surviving
and he doesn't care who he has to kill or

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:01.420
steal from in order to do it.

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:05.230
However there is still a symbol that ties
him back to his old life and that is the watch

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.780
that Sarah gave him on the night she died.

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:11.739
Though it's busted up and broken he still
wears it because it's the singular memory

00:04:11.739 --> 00:04:13.080
of his daughter that remains.

00:04:13.080 --> 00:04:18.000
The cracks in it very much represent his own
psyche and how beneath the surface he still

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.860
longs for a realtionship like the one he had
with his daughter.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.030
Now this very much becomes the case in Ellie.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:28.220
Revealed to be immune to the Cordyseps infection
she represents the hope that humanity can

00:04:28.220 --> 00:04:32.670
find a cure and return to the old life that
everyone likely longs for.

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:36.699
Joel and Tess are tasked with escorting her
across the country to a firefly outpost and

00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:40.389
we watch as Joel slowly lowers his walls in
order to let her in.

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:43.900
Ellie represents the daughter that he lost
and the chance to return back to a normal

00:04:43.900 --> 00:04:46.110
life like what he had with Sarah.

00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:50.030
There's so many subtle moments in the game
and I love the moment where Joel longingly

00:04:50.030 --> 00:04:53.910
stares at his watch almost as if to remind
himself of that life.

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:57.570
There's also the fact that he called Sarah
Baby Girl which is something that he later

00:04:57.570 --> 00:05:06.219
refers to Ellie as.

00:05:06.219 --> 00:05:07.219
-

00:05:07.219 --> 00:05:17.570
After Tess is killed we see Joel refusing
to talk about it or acknowledge it because

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:21.361
to him it's something else that he won't have
to face up to if he pushes it to the back

00:05:21.361 --> 00:05:22.361
of his mind.

00:05:22.361 --> 00:05:26.871
However he very clearly becomes attached to
Ellie and he even refuses to palm her off

00:05:26.871 --> 00:05:27.871
to his brother Tommy.

00:05:27.871 --> 00:05:32.000
Now at his outpost we get a very important
scene in which Tommy says that he returned

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.449
back to their homes in Austin Texas.

00:05:33.449 --> 00:05:36.780
The night that the outbreak happened they
had to make a run for it and didn't get the

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.440
chance to grab any personal belongings.

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:43.430
Joel hasn't returned because of how painful
it is to go back there and thus it's all remained

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:45.870
pretty much how he left it.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:49.940
Unless someones been through it and spammed
the triangle button on every square inch of

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.039
the place.

00:05:51.039 --> 00:05:52.039
Guilty.

00:05:52.039 --> 00:05:55.690
Anyway here Tommy found a photograph of Joel
and Sarah but he refuses to really acknowledge

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:57.970
it and he immediately hands it back.

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:01.419
However come the end of the game we learn
that Ellie grabbed this on their way out and

00:06:01.419 --> 00:06:03.470
that she's carried it with her ever since.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:17.389
She gives it to Joel and he longingly looks
at it before saying.

00:06:17.389 --> 00:06:18.389
-

00:06:18.389 --> 00:06:31.000
Now this is clearly a major change in him.

00:06:31.000 --> 00:06:34.900
Rather than refusing to even acknowledge it
he puts it in his pocket and finally lets

00:06:34.900 --> 00:06:36.211
that part of his life back in.

00:06:36.211 --> 00:06:40.840
Now this moment is very important for both
Joel and Ellie as it's also the last major

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:44.870
conversation that they have before they're
quote unquote saved by the fireflies.

00:06:44.870 --> 00:06:50.090
The pair make their way underground and after
almost drowning the pair are taken to a hospital

00:06:50.090 --> 00:06:52.319
where they've made their camp.

00:06:52.319 --> 00:06:56.210
Joel wakes up to discover that they're preparing
Ellie for surgery so that they can remove

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:59.949
the mutated strain from her which will finally
give us the hope for a cure.

00:06:59.949 --> 00:07:04.889
There's just one thing, Ellie will die during
the procedure and in order to save humanity

00:07:04.889 --> 00:07:06.620
they have to kill her.

00:07:06.620 --> 00:07:11.850
Joel doesn't get the chance to say goodbye
and instead he's escorted away by an armed

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:12.850
guard.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:16.710
At this point he pulls a fast one and kills
the soldier before brutally interrogating

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:19.160
him so that he can go and save her.

00:07:19.160 --> 00:07:24.129
Now though this is completely damning humanity,
we understand Joel completely in this moment.

00:07:24.129 --> 00:07:28.030
Like him we've become attached to Ellie throughout
the story and after spending a good ten hours

00:07:28.030 --> 00:07:32.039
protecting her the last thing that we want
to see her do is die.

00:07:32.039 --> 00:07:36.120
In addition to this we've seen the ugly side
of humanity throughout and obviously question

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:40.300
whether we're even worth saving if the cost
is going to be one of the only genuinely good

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:42.610
characters that we meet.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:45.879
It's said that children are our future and
I think it's smart to have the game centre

00:07:45.879 --> 00:07:50.340
around middle aged and elderly characters
because it shows how f**ked humanity is.

00:07:50.340 --> 00:07:55.259
Sarah, Sam and Ellie are the only child characters
in the game and to have all three die could

00:07:55.259 --> 00:07:58.819
completely kill the outlook that there's a
bright future ahead of us.

00:07:58.819 --> 00:08:02.500
Even if players were given a dialogue tree
during this moment where we could decide what

00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:07.220
to do I still think that the majority of people
would choose to save Ellie.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:10.490
The final part of the game follows him as
we move through the hospital murdering the

00:08:10.490 --> 00:08:14.490
Fireflies and what's probably the last brain
surgeons on the planet.

00:08:14.490 --> 00:08:19.370
But you understand all of this because you've
been with Ellie and will do anything to stop

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:20.990
her from being killed.

00:08:20.990 --> 00:08:25.370
You succeed as well and manage to make it
out of the hospital killing Marlene on the

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:26.370
way out.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:30.470
She very much represents the opposite side
of the coin to Joel due to the backstory that

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:34.490
we get filled in we know that she also cared
about Ellie as well.

00:08:34.490 --> 00:08:39.560
She was entrusted to her but Marlene is willing
to make the tough choice for the greater good.

00:08:39.560 --> 00:08:43.891
The needs of the many outweigh the needs of
the few to her and the pair very much represent

00:08:43.891 --> 00:08:46.070
a dichotomy over what to do.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:50.110
Knowing that they won't stop coming for Ellie
he kills her in a scene and it shows just

00:08:50.110 --> 00:08:53.880
how low he is willing to sink to protect Ellie.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:58.050
It's very important to bear in mind that almost
everytime we see Marlene she's wounded and

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.050
cowering over.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:03.589
This is very much the case in her final scene
and she paints out a sympathetic figure as

00:09:03.589 --> 00:09:05.990
she lies on the ground begging for her life.

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:10.519
But Joel can't have Ellie with a target on
her back and thus he does what he has to in

00:09:10.519 --> 00:09:12.390
order to make sure Ellie is safe.

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:16.441
Now this entire flashback is told to us with
the backdrop of Ellie waking up in the back

00:09:16.441 --> 00:09:19.350
of a car still in her hospital gown.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:23.040
Joel peddals her a story about how there's
lots of immune people out there and how the

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:25.540
fireflies have stopped looking for a cure.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:30.530
The story doesn't even really make sense especially
due to her still being in her hospital gown.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:34.880
Ellie is still too devastated to question
it though and she turns around defeated that

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:36.570
it's all been for nothing.

00:09:36.570 --> 00:09:40.579
This is a moment that really stands out to
me and if we cut back to the Giraffe scene

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:44.850
Ellie ends up storming off because Joel offers
her a chance to return to Tommy's.

00:09:44.850 --> 00:09:48.500
She says that it can't be for nothing and
that they have to power ahead.

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:52.820
Now when you think about it, the entire cure
storyline that youve spent the last how ever

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:57.230
many hours pushing through has been completely
pointless and you'd have been better off just

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.690
staying at Tommys in the mid point of the
game.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:03.620
However that's never really crossed my mind
until this video because I've been so wrapped

00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:05.160
up in the characters.

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:10.010
Even with the ending I still feel like it's
a triumphant one because you saved Ellie and

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:14.330
Joel finally took a step back towards humanity
rather than being the closed a cut off person

00:10:14.330 --> 00:10:15.330
that he was.

00:10:15.330 --> 00:10:18.920
Now they could easily end the game there and
I don't think many people would've been mad

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:20.130
if that had been the case.

00:10:20.130 --> 00:10:25.279
We'd just had a major action scene, stopped
Ellie from being hunted and were riding off

00:10:25.279 --> 00:10:26.279
into the sunset.

00:10:26.279 --> 00:10:30.060
But The Last Of Us adds an epilogue that makes
it's ending something that will stick with

00:10:30.060 --> 00:10:32.649
everyone long after they put the controller
down.

00:10:32.649 --> 00:10:36.380
We don't know how big of a time jump there's
been inbetween the car ride and where we end

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:38.959
up but clearly some time has passed.

00:10:38.959 --> 00:10:45.170
Juxtaposing the dynanmics that we've had throughout,
Joel is way more talkative and instead Ellie

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:48.250
is now the reserved one.

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:53.310
Eventually she stops him and brings up the
day that she got bitten and how her friend

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:55.839
Riley wasn't lucky enough to make it.

00:10:55.839 --> 00:10:59.911
This is something that is later explored in
the left behind DLC and it's clear that she

00:10:59.911 --> 00:11:01.950
suffers from survivors guilt.

00:11:01.950 --> 00:11:06.220
Joel mirrors this as well and he says that
he struggled along time with surviving.

00:11:06.220 --> 00:11:10.320
This is clearly commenting on how he died
instead of Sarah and he even touches the watch

00:11:10.320 --> 00:11:13.389
for a second to signify the guilt that he
felt being someone who walked away that day

00:11:13.389 --> 00:11:14.389
whilst Sarah didn't.

00:11:14.389 --> 00:11:18.870
However he says that you find something to
fight for and Ellie very much represents this.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.740
Had she died then we know that Joel would
have also have been robbed of his purpose

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:24.100
and that he'd be surviving with nothing to
survive for.

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:28.700
Now on top of this she's clearly been thinking
about the fateful day a lot and she asks Joel

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:58.250
flat out whether everything he said is true
or not.

00:11:58.250 --> 00:11:59.250
-

00:11:59.250 --> 00:12:01.279
Joel looks her dead in the eyes and swears
that it was all true.

00:12:01.279 --> 00:12:05.490
Now I'm sure that a lot of you growing up
were told by your parents to tell them the

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:10.270
truth and they'd make you look them directly
in the eyes and do it to see if you were being

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:11.700
genuine or not.

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:17.190
This is normally seen as being a sign of honesty
however as humans get older we of course become

00:12:17.190 --> 00:12:19.529
aware of this and adapt it into our lies.

00:12:19.529 --> 00:12:23.410
It's actually said by psychologists that if
someone does this that they're more likely

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:28.420
to be lying because it's practiced and we
know that it's meant to convey honesty so

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:29.420
we purposely do it

00:12:29.420 --> 00:12:35.199
As we know, Joel is lying here and thus him
doing this also lets us know how manipulative

00:12:35.199 --> 00:12:36.199
he is.

00:12:36.199 --> 00:12:40.380
All that remains is Ellie's reaction which
conveys so much.

00:12:40.380 --> 00:12:41.380
-

00:12:41.380 --> 00:12:45.650
I absolutely love the way this plays out and
as her eyes glance about we can read doubt,

00:12:45.650 --> 00:12:47.649
suspicion and confusion.

00:12:47.649 --> 00:12:51.890
She's clearly built up in her head that he's
lying but he's potentially willing to lie

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:56.050
on top of the lie because he doesn't want
to change the situation between them.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:59.649
Ellie knows that if he's lying then he was
willing to murder people just to save her

00:12:59.649 --> 00:13:02.959
life and she's clearly conflicted because
of this.

00:13:02.959 --> 00:13:05.930
Now she has a couple of choices here.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:09.730
Either she can say he's lying and this will
divide them further.

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:13.560
Or she can accept the lies and live in a world
where she won't have to deal with the survivors

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:17.840
guilt or truth that someone murdered people
to save her.

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:21.330
It's a tough thing to deal with and she simply
utters the word okay.

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:26.150
It's not really an acceptance or denial of
anything and instead she's just taking everything

00:13:26.150 --> 00:13:29.889
at face value because the truth of it is far
more horrifying.

00:13:29.889 --> 00:13:33.880
Now though I'm spouting off things that are
basically my opinion here it's completely

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:37.760
possible to take your own interpretation of
Ellie's thoughts at this point.

00:13:37.760 --> 00:13:42.250
The game really wants the player to make up
their own mind and everyone will have their

00:13:42.250 --> 00:13:43.380
own reading on this moment.

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:47.501
Personally I do see Ellie as being someone
that knows the truth because of the way that

00:13:47.501 --> 00:13:52.790
Joel acts but she's willing to bury it because
she simply doesn't want to accept the reality.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:56.200
Joel has been someone that has done horrendous
things in order to survive and now we see

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:59.820
Ellie willing to accept a lie in order to
do the same thing.

00:13:59.820 --> 00:14:04.790
So much is given to us in this moment and
it's why the game stands the test of time.

00:14:04.790 --> 00:14:08.810
Naughty Dog can release a remake of the game
that is completely the same as the original

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:11.180
because they don't need to change anything.

00:14:11.180 --> 00:14:15.600
The story is what carries this and this final
scene that haunts players is a reason that

